  "proof": "by\n  intro G H g h f hf x y z hxy\n  rw [hf x z, hf y z, hxy]\n",
  "bridge": "The original goal asks whether right multiplication by z preserves equality of the two images when testing membership in the fibre over h.one. Rewriting both product images using the raw homomorphism hypothesis hf reduces the two sides to h.mul (f x) (f z) = h.one and h.mul (f y) (f z) = h.one. The supplied equality hxy identifies these propositions. No candidate property is used: kernel_mul requires separate kernel-membership hypotheses, which are not supplied here, and bundling f and hf as Theory.Hom would only repeat the available multiplication law. The proof remains in the original vocabulary. Packaging does not run Lean or establish verification."
}

